onetheless - also &quot;misunderstood&quot; Marx?<br /> <br /> Why do you think that EVERY single Marxist intellectual is a genocidal maniac? Do you think this is an accident?<br /> <br /> Oh, there's also another good video:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/hj6lvtCl6C0\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/hj6lvtCl6C0\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://youtu.be/hj6lvtCl6C0\" target=\"_blank\"> https://youtu.be/hj6lvtCl6C0 </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> &quot;Executions: yes, we have executed. We executed, and we will keep executing for as long as necessary.&quot; - Ernesto &quot;Che&quot; Guevara, UN Assembly, 1964.<br /> <br /> Here's another &quot;hero&quot; of the left, Che Guevara, the murderer of children.<br /> <br /> Now, why is it that marxists always worship eugenists and murderers? Is it just a coincidence?<br /> <br /> Just think about it for a little. And before doubting my words, be careful to note that Im showing you those men defending their atrocious views from their own mouths, so there's no margin for doubt. This is what marxism is: a murderous ideology.<br /> <br /> Now, I'll soon show you the sources about Karl Marx himself, dont you worry. I just wanted to show the sort of &quot;disciples&quot; that the &quot;saint&quot; Karl Marx managed to attract, and I want you to seriously think why is that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T10:07:56-07:00","id":1483881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445889-thoughts-about-victorian-mage?p=1483751#post1483751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, while I'm not a Marxist myself, I've read Marx and never found any of those instruction to build murderous totalitarian states. Care to share sources, so I can read them?</div> </div> </div> </div>In march 22nd, 1853, Karl Marx wrote in an article published in the \u201cNew York Daily Tribune\u201d, in which he criticizes the development of capitalism (words in bold by me):<br /> <br /> <i>Society is undergoing a silent revolution, which must be submitted to, and which takes no more notice of the human existences it breaks down than an earthquake regards the houses it subverts. <b>The classes and the races, too weak to master the new conditions of life, must give way.</b> But can there be anything more puerile, more short-sighted, than the views of those Economists who believe in all earnest that this woeful transitory state means nothing but adapting society to the acquisitive propensities of capitalists, both landlords and money-lords? In Great Britain the working of that process is most transparent. The application of modern science to production clears the land of its inhabitants, but it concentrates people in manufacturing towns.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> In another article, written in 1849, Friedrich Engels (Marx\u2019s intellectual partner) talks about the 1848 revolutions, the role of the nations involved, and how people used to be oppressed become counter-revolutionary:<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;How did this division of the nations come about, what was its basis?<br /> <br /> The division is in accordance with all the previous history of the nationalities in question. It is the beginning of the decision on the life or death of all these nations, large and small.<br /> <br /> All the earlier history of Austria up to the present day is proof of this and 1848 confirmed it. Among all the large and small nations of Austria, only three standard-bearers of progress took an active part in history, and still retain their vitality \u2014 the Germans, the Poles and the Magyars. Hence they are now revolutionary.<br /> <br /> All the other large and small nationalities and peoples are <b>destined to perish before long in the revolutionary world storm</b>. For that reason they are now counter-revolutionary&quot;</i><br /> <br /> Yes, the quote from the documentary &quot;Soviet Story&quot; from 2008 and precise; hardly their fault thou, since they picked that from a source from 1976 that mixed and altered those parts togheter; so they picked a bad source.<br /> <br /> That doesnt change the fact that both Marx and Engels are CLEARLY defending VIOLENT revolution in both of this texts. Surely they have been misrepresented, but the original quotes and with their full context arent so much better either.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T10:44:01-07:00","id":1483884,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445889-thoughts-about-victorian-mage?p=1483751#post1483751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, while I'm not a Marxist myself, I've read Marx and never found any of those instruction to build murderous totalitarian states. Care to share sources, so I can read them?</div> </div> </div> </div>Would the Enciclopedia Britannica be a good enough source for you?<br /> <br /> &quot;Dictatorship of the proletariat, in Marxism... originally was conceived by Karl Marx (1818\u201383) as a dictatorship by the majority class. Because Marx regarded all governments as class dictatorships, he viewed proletarian dictatorship as no worse than any other form of government...&quot;<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.britannica.com/topic/revisionism-Marxism\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.britannica.com/topic/revisionism-Marxism</a><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> &quot;The phrase \u2018dictatorship of the proletariat\u2019 first appeared in a series of articles by Marx, later titled The Class Struggles in France 1848-1850, published in what was then Marx\u2019s own London magazine. The first article, written in January 1850, came off the press in early March. The expression or its equivalent appeared not once but three times \u2013 in each of the three installments (or chapters) that comprised the original series...&quot;[/i]<br /> <br /> <i>&quot;...This is, the concept which Marx summarized as \u201cpermanent (that is, ongoing or continuous) revolution,\u201d \u201ca revolution which does not come to a halt until the proletariat has taken power.\u201d It is this conclusion that introduced the question of proletarian power (or, same thing, proletarian \u2018dictatorship\u2019) into Marx\u2019s writings of 1850 analyzing the defeated revolution...</i><br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.marxists.org/subject/marxmyths/hal-draper/article2.htm\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.marxists.org/subject/marxmyths/hal-draper/article2.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> The 'Dictatorship of the Proletariat' in Marx and Engels by Hal Draper 1987 </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.marxists.org/subject/marxmyths/hal-draper/article2.htm\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.marxists.org/subject/marxmyths/hal-draper/article2.htm </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> The one above is interesting. It's from a <b>Marxist</b> site, so perhaps if you believe that the Encyclopedia Britannica is &quot;biased&quot;, maybe you would give more thought to the opinions of marxists themselves. In this, they dont try to deny even for a second that Marx defended the &quot;Dictatorship of the Proletariat&quot; nor that he wanted violent revolution to usher in his paradise filled with horrors - which is what ALL of his adepts followed TO THE LETTER.<br /> <br /> Instead, the Marxists here try to show how wonderful and filled of love the dictatorship of Marx was supposed to be.<br /> <br /> That's a good reading to begin with. Enjoy. And Awake. Marxism is DEATH.<br /> <br /> Is that enough for sources for now?<br /> <br /> I wont even tell you what kind of a man Marx was. He were sustained his own life by his parents, by his wife and by his friend Engels, because he never worked in his life. <br /> <br /> When his father died, he said he had no time to waste going to the funeral, only to come begging to his mom for forgiveness when she got so disappointed that she treatned to cut his allowance.<br /> <br /> When Engels' father, the man who paid for the playboy Engels good life AND for Marx, Marx criticized his friend for going to the funeral, only to go begging for forgiveness when Engels too treatened to cut his allowance.<br /> <br /> And his wife, his third source of income, he cheated on with their housekeeper, having a bastard child with her - whom by the way Marx treated as a dog, not even allowing the child to sit at the table with his other siblings.<br /> <br /> This child ended up dying due to mistreatment. 2 of the legitimate daughters of Marx would eventually commit suicide.<br /> <br /> <br /> THIS is the greatest hero of the Left, the great prophet of the leftist &quot;Paradise&quot;: Karl Marx, the inhuman monster.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24689-kakost","name":"Kakost","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"586"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-06-13T11:03:22-07:00","id":1483886,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1445889-thoughts-about-victorian-mage?p=1483751#post1483751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Interestingly, while I'm not a Marxist myself, I've read Marx and never found any of those instruction to build murderous totalitarian states. Care to share sources, so I can read them?</div> </div> </div> </div>And to end this boring topic once and for all:<br /> <br /> Hitler's Lebensraum, the &quot;Shrinking Markets&quot; theory of his &quot;Mein Kampfy&quot; book and it's connection to marxism:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://nationalinterest.org/feature/why-hitler-wanted-conquer-new-%E2%80%98lebensraum-east%E2%80%99-188255\" target=\"_blank\">https://nationalinterest.org/feature...2%80%99-188255</a><br /> <br /> Have you ever heard about the &quot;Shrinking Markets&quot; theory, an &quot;economic&quot; theory defended by Hitler in his &quot;Mein Kampf&quot; book?<br /> <br /> I bet you have not, which is strange since the entire reasoning for &quot;Lebensraum&quot; which has lead to WW2 is because of this theory.<br /> <br /> And you wanna know why you have never heard about this?<br /> <br /> Because if you had, you would know that Hitler's &quot;Shrinking Markets&quot; is EXACTLY the same as Karl Marx's economic theory of &quot;The tendency of the rate of profit to fall&quot;, which is the reason why Hitler wanted &quot;Lebensraum&quot;, to create an <b>Autarky</b>, which by the way is ALSO what the USSR wanted, to be an Autarky - self sufficient country.<br /> <br /> So, if you wanted to see why Nazism and Socialism are indeed CLOSELY related, that's the first point for you to begin.<br /> <br /> And now I've already given you VAST sources to why Karl Marx and his ideology are utterly evil and despicable in every possible sense, I hope that's enough to show you the truth - the same truth I had to contend with some time ago. Karl Marx was a monster and marxism is pure evil. It is just as evil as nazism itself in every possible way.<br /> <br /> And now I would prefer to end it here, I dont particularly enjoy touching those subjects, let alone when I just want to have fun with my favour